e_Extra-Terrestrial.htm"}, {"title": "E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial", "url": "https://bafybeiemxf5abjwjbikoz4mc3a3dla6ual3jsgpdr4cjr3oz3evfyavhwq.ipfs.4everland.io/wiki/E.T..html"}, {"title": "E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial", "url": "https://kaweah.freedombox.rocks/kiwix/wikipedia_en_all_maxi_2023-10/E.T."}, {"title": "42 Years Later: The Exact Date E.T. The Extra-Terrestrial Came Out And Why It Still Matters", "url": "https://slbubble.studentbridge.com/celebnews032/42-years-later-the-exact-date-et-the-extra-terrestrial-came-out-and-why-it-still-matters-q4gsb.html"}, {"title": "Checked content", "url": "https://rachel.core2learn.org/modules/en-wikipedia_for_schools-static/wp/e/E.T._the_Extra-Terrestrial.htm"}, {"title": "E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial", "url": "https://simple.wikipedia.com/wiki/E.T."}]}, "The U.S. theatrical release was June 11, 1982, distributed by Universal Pictures.\n\n- **Cannes premiere:** May 26, 1982 (Cannes), where the film premiered as the closing film of the Cannes Film Festival.\n- **U.S. release:** Wikipedia lists June 11, 1982 (United States), and a fan-oriented retrospective gives the same date as Original U.S. Theatrical Release: June 11, 1982.\n- **Note:** One result (a doral.edu page) also gives June 11, 1982, but it looks like a low-quality site, so I'd rely on the Wikipedia mirrors and the retrospective for confirmation."], "durationSeconds": 5.633096916999999, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01S8mDgVk8MuU6YGdrbSvQwX", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_011qasaZN3gAzbSiwEekZ1AG", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I_Think_I%27m_Go_Go\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argybargy\"}, {\"url\": \"https://Www.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argybargy\"}, {\"url\": \"https://mag.highresaudio.com/album/view/iayppz/squeeze-argybargy-remastered\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.deezer.com/album/104903\"}, {\"url\": \"https://bestclassicbands.com/squeeze-argybargy-review-6-8-233/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://bestclassicbands.com/squeeze-argybargy-review-6-8-23\"}, {\"url\": \"https://streaming.highresaudio.com/album/view/iayppz/squeeze-argybargy-remastered\"}, {\"url\": \"https://kwx.liehendr.com/content/wikipedia_en_all_maxi_2024-01/A/Argybargy\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:58:44.678Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Squeeze \"I Think I'm Go Go\" song Argybargy 1980", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01AXhNpJjpPGPmHWg5x4VNSZ", "content": [{"title": "I Think I%27m Go Go", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I_Think_I%27m_Go_Go"}, {"title": "Argybargy", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argybargy"}, {"title": "www.wikipedia.org", "url": "https://Www.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argybargy"}, {"title": "Argybargy (Remastered) Squeeze", "url": "https://mag.highresaudio.com/album/view/iayppz/squeeze-argybargy-remastered"}, {"title": "1980 | UMC (Universal Music Catalogue)", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/album/104903"}, {"title": "RECENT POSTS", "url": "https://bestclassicbands.com/squeeze-argybargy-review-6-8-233/"}, {"title": "Squeeze and Their Hook-Filled ‘Argybargy’", "url": "https://bestclassicbands.com/squeeze-argybargy-review-6-8-23"}, {"title": "Argybargy (Remastered) Squeeze", "url": "https://streaming.highresaudio.com/album/view/iayppz/squeeze-argybargy-remastered"}, {"title": "kwx.liehendr.com", "url": "https://kwx.liehendr.com/content/wikipedia_en_all_maxi_2024-01/A/Argybargy"}]}, "\"I Think I'm Go Go\" is a track on Squeeze's third album, Argybargy, which came out in February 1980. Both the song and album are credited to Chris Difford and Glenn Tilbrook, and John Wood and the band produced it.\n\n- **Origin of the title:** Difford has said the song is about the strain of touring, and that the phrase was a band expression of the time for the disorientation of life on the road. [1-1, 1-2, 1-3]\n- **Setting:** Difford described the verses as covering Amsterdam, New York, and London. [1-5, 1-8, 1-9]\n- **Album placement:** It closes the original LP's side one, and its runtime is listed at about 4:16 on the standard edition, though other listings give longer versions. [7-10, 4-7, 9-21]\n- **Sound:** A review describes an arrangement with string parts by Del Newman, plus synthesizer and unusual percussion, with Difford adding vocal parts to Tilbrook's lead. [7-11, 7-12]\n- **Context:** Argybargy was the band's first album to chart in the US, reaching number 71 on the Billboard 200. [3-3]\n\nI didn't reproduce any lyrics. Sources for the details above are Wikipedia, a Deezer catalogue listing, and a BestClassicBands review."], "durationSeconds": 6.9567375, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_011qasaZN3gAzbSiwEekZ1AG", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgDXdpyfJVZJvPENjWocs", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**答案：大约 2 年。**\n\n- Squeeze 的《I Think I'm Go Go》收在第三张专辑 *Argybargy* 里，专辑 1980 年 2 月发行。\n- 《E.T. 外星人》1982 年 5 月 26 日在戛纳电影节首映，1982 年 6 月 11 日在美国上映。\n\n1980 年到 1982 年，相隔 2 年。从 1980 年 2 月算到 1982 年 6 月，大约是 2 年 4 个月。\n\n一共搜了 2 次。\n\n依据：\n- [I Think I'm Go Go – Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I_Think_I%27m_Go_Go)\n- [Argybargy – Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argybargy)\n- [E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial – Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E.T._the_Extra-Terrestrial)"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2326, "cache_read_input_tokens": 4311, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 2326}, "output_tokens": 343, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:58:48.861Z", "request_id": "req_011CgDXdpKDvwv2XieX2skau"}
